---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"For Lenders' Counsel: Selling the Loan in a Receivership"} description={"When the lender would prefer to be paid now: we purchase the note with the receivership in place, substitute in as plaintiff, and work with the receiver through to a sale."}>
  <Hero eyebrow={"For receivers and counsel"} title={"When the lender would prefer to sell the loan."} lead={"A receivership can run for a long time before a sale closes. Some lenders decide partway through that they would prefer to be paid now."} />
  <SectionNav section="receivers" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap intro">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">For lender's counsel</p><h2>We purchase the note with the receivership in place.</h2>
        <div class="body"><p>We substitute in as plaintiff, and work with the receiver through to a sale.</p></div></div>
      <dl class="pillars">
        <div><dt>No interruption</dt><dd>The receiver and manager remain in place under the existing order.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>One closing</dt><dd>The lender is paid at the loan sale and has no further role in the case.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Advances addressed</dt><dd>Protective advances and receivership costs to date are accounted for in the price.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">How it works</p><h2>From the lender's decision to the end of its role.</h2></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>The lender decides to sell</h3><p>Partway through the case, the lender prefers to be paid now.</p></li>
        <li><h3>We purchase the note</h3><p>The sale is made with the receivership in place. The receiver and manager continue under the existing order.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Substitution as plaintiff</h3><p>We substitute in as plaintiff in the foreclosure action, following the court's practice.</p></li>
        <li><h3>We work with the receiver</h3><p>The case goes forward through to a sale of the hotel.</p></li>
        <li><h3>The lender is finished</h3><p>The lender is paid at the loan sale and has no further role in the case.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Points counsel commonly address</p><h2>What goes into a loan sale in this posture.</h2>
        <p>General points, offered as a checklist. Each case has its own order, its own court, and its own documents.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>The documents</h3><p>The note, with its endorsement or <a href="/glossary/#allonge">allonge</a>, and the <a href="/glossary/#assignment-of-mortgage">assignment of mortgage</a>, which is recorded.</p></div>
        <div><h3>The case</h3><p>Notice to the court and the parties, and the motion to substitute the new holder as plaintiff.</p></div>
        <div><h3>The receiver</h3><p>The receiver and manager stay in place under the order. The receiver's reports continue.</p></div>
        <div><h3>The numbers</h3><p>Protective advances and receivership costs to date, accounted for in the price.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Consents</h3><p>If the loan carries a government guarantee, the agency's consent requirements for a sale apply.</p></div>
        <div><h3>The file</h3><p>The order of appointment, the receiver's reports, and the status of the foreclosure action are where we start.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/receivers/what-we-ask-for/">Information that lets us respond <span>Receivers</span></a></li><li><a href="/library/choices/">Extend, sell, or foreclose <span>Library</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#protective-advance">Protective advance <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#note-sale">Note sale (loan sale) <span>Glossary</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Tell us about the hotel and the case."} text={"We respond to receivers and counsel directly."} label={"Discuss a receivership"} />
</Base>
